1
00:00:03,433 --> 00:00:05,266
I'm Peppa Pig. [snorts]

2
00:00:05,333 --> 00:00:08,033
-This is my little brother, George.
-[George snorts]

3
00:00:08,100 --> 00:00:10,299
-This is Mommy Pig.
-[Mommy Pig snorts]

4
00:00:10,366 --> 00:00:11,799
And this is Daddy Pig.

5
00:00:12,033 --> 00:00:14,200
-[Daddy Pig snorts]
-[all laugh]

6
00:00:14,266 --> 00:00:15,766
Peppa Pig. [snorts]

7
00:00:18,666 --> 00:00:20,533
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

8
00:00:20,599 --> 00:00:21,466
[horn honks]

9
00:00:21,533 --> 00:00:24,000
[narrator] Peppa and George
are having a sleepover

10
00:00:24,066 --> 00:00:25,700
at Granny and Grandpa's house.

11
00:00:25,766 --> 00:00:28,799
-Granny Pig!
-Gangy Ig!

12
00:00:29,033 --> 00:00:30,566
Hello, my little ones.

13
00:00:30,633 --> 00:00:32,566
Bye-bye. See you later.

14
00:00:32,633 --> 00:00:34,566
-Bye-bye, Mommy.
-[George snorts]

15
00:00:34,633 --> 00:00:35,500
[horn honks]

16
00:00:35,566 --> 00:00:38,100
Come and see where you're going
to sleep tonight.

17
00:00:38,166 --> 00:00:40,166
[Peppa &amp; George giggling]

18
00:00:42,066 --> 00:00:44,699
This was Mommy Pig's room
when she was little.

19
00:00:44,766 --> 00:00:46,766
In olden times.

20
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:49,266
And this is the bed Mommy slept on.

21
00:00:49,333 --> 00:00:51,500
Ooh, bouncy bed.

22
00:00:51,566 --> 00:00:53,533
[Peppa &amp; George giggling]

23
00:00:55,599 --> 00:00:58,366
You're like your mommy
when she was little.

24
00:00:58,433 --> 00:01:01,766
-[snorts] Did Mommy bounce on the bed?
-Of course.

25
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:05,566
But Mommy tells us
not to bounce on the beds.

26
00:01:05,633 --> 00:01:09,333
[snorts] When Mommy was little,
she was cheeky like you.

27
00:01:09,399 --> 00:01:10,466
Was she?

28
00:01:10,533 --> 00:01:12,366
-[chuckles] Yes.
[both giggle]

29
00:01:12,433 --> 00:01:15,533
Now, let's go and see Grandpa Pig
in the garden.

30
00:01:15,600 --> 00:01:17,166
[Peppa &amp; George giggling]

31
00:01:19,233 --> 00:01:22,166
-Grandpa Pig!
-Baba Ig.

32
00:01:22,233 --> 00:01:25,500
[snorts] Hello, Peppa. Hello, George.

33
00:01:25,566 --> 00:01:27,600
Come and see my carrots.

34
00:01:28,233 --> 00:01:31,100
[narrator] Grandpa Pig is very proud
of his vegetables.

35
00:01:31,166 --> 00:01:32,266
[Peppa &amp; George] Ooh.

36
00:01:32,333 --> 00:01:34,800
And here are my peas.

37
00:01:35,033 --> 00:01:36,133
[Peppa &amp; George] Ahh.

38
00:01:36,199 --> 00:01:38,800
But best of all are my lettuces.

39
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:41,533
Oh, no!

40
00:01:41,600 --> 00:01:43,666
My lettuces!

41
00:01:43,733 --> 00:01:47,399
I think the birds have eaten them,
Grandpa.

42
00:01:47,466 --> 00:01:49,333
Yes. Birds.

43
00:01:49,399 --> 00:01:52,800
Why didn't Mr. Scarecrow scare them away?

44
00:01:53,033 --> 00:01:58,366
Because the birds that ate my lettuces
are very stupid. [snorts]

45
00:01:58,433 --> 00:02:00,133
What's the matter?

46
00:02:00,199 --> 00:02:04,000
Your friends have been eating
my vegetables again.

47
00:02:04,066 --> 00:02:07,000
-Which friends?
-Tom, Dick and Harry.

48
00:02:07,066 --> 00:02:08,000
[chickens clucking]

49
00:02:08,066 --> 00:02:09,500
Those aren't their names.

50
00:02:10,133 --> 00:02:11,766
[narrator] Granny Pig has chickens.

51
00:02:12,466 --> 00:02:13,566
Wow!

52
00:02:13,633 --> 00:02:17,333
Say hello to Jemima, Sarah and Vanessa.

53
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:19,066
-Hello.
-[George snorts]

54
00:02:19,133 --> 00:02:21,033
And here is Neville.

55
00:02:21,100 --> 00:02:23,000
[crows]

56
00:02:23,066 --> 00:02:25,366
Is Neville a boy chicken?

57
00:02:25,433 --> 00:02:27,400
Yes, Peppa, he's a cockerel.

58
00:02:27,466 --> 00:02:29,299
[snorts] He's the worst.

59
00:02:29,366 --> 00:02:31,466
Scratching up my vegetables.

60
00:02:31,533 --> 00:02:33,500
[Granny Pig] Neville wouldn't hurt a fly.

61
00:02:33,566 --> 00:02:35,766
[Grandpa Pig] I've seen him eat flies.

62
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:37,000
[Peppa &amp; George] Ew!

63
00:02:37,066 --> 00:02:39,600
And he ate my lettuce.

64
00:02:39,666 --> 00:02:43,433
You don't want to eat Grandpa's lettuce,
do you?

65
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:44,633
[chickens clucking]

66
00:02:44,700 --> 00:02:47,566
Not when there's lovely corn to eat.

67
00:02:48,200 --> 00:02:50,366
Come on. This way home.

68
00:02:52,066 --> 00:02:55,533
Peppa, George, would you like
to feed corn to the chickens?

69
00:02:55,600 --> 00:02:57,299
Yes, please, Granny.

70
00:02:58,299 --> 00:02:59,299
[George snorts]

71
00:02:59,366 --> 00:03:01,533
Here you are, chickens. [snorts] Eat up.

72
00:03:03,799 --> 00:03:06,600
Ooh, you've got a Wendy house.

73
00:03:06,666 --> 00:03:10,433
That's the chicken coop.
It's where the chickens lay their eggs.

74
00:03:10,500 --> 00:03:14,066
Eggs? I can't see any eggs.

75
00:03:14,533 --> 00:03:16,799
Not now, but there will be eggs soon.

76
00:03:17,033 --> 00:03:18,066
[Peppa &amp; George] Ooh.

77
00:03:20,299 --> 00:03:22,466
[narrator] It is bedtime for Peppa
and George

78
00:03:22,533 --> 00:03:24,666
at Granny and Grandpa's house.

79
00:03:24,733 --> 00:03:26,466
[both giggling]

80
00:03:26,533 --> 00:03:29,633
Have the chickens laid their eggs yet,
Granny?

81
00:03:29,700 --> 00:03:33,700
-Maybe in the morning, Peppa.
-How will we know when it's morning?

82
00:03:33,766 --> 00:03:35,166
Neville will tell us.

83
00:03:35,633 --> 00:03:37,033
Now, go to sleep.

84
00:03:37,100 --> 00:03:38,700
[Peppa &amp; George] Night, night.

85
00:03:38,766 --> 00:03:40,766
[Peppa &amp; George snoring]

86
00:03:44,466 --> 00:03:45,733
[narrator] It is morning.

87
00:03:45,799 --> 00:03:46,666
[both snoring]

88
00:03:46,733 --> 00:03:48,200
[Neville crows]

89
00:03:48,266 --> 00:03:49,766
It's Neville!

90
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:52,000
[Peppa &amp; George giggling]

91
00:03:54,033 --> 00:03:56,666
[snorts] Thank you
for waking us up, Neville.

92
00:03:56,733 --> 00:03:58,566
[crows]

93
00:03:58,633 --> 00:04:02,166
[giggles] Cock-a-doodle-doo! [laughs]

94
00:04:02,233 --> 00:04:04,666
Good morning, Jemima, Sarah and Vanessa.

95
00:04:05,266 --> 00:04:09,766
-Do you have any eggs for us?
-One, two, three, four.

96
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:11,566
Four eggs, Granny.

97
00:04:11,633 --> 00:04:14,100
Now we'll have eggs for breakfast.

98
00:04:14,166 --> 00:04:19,233
Thank you, Jemima, Sarah and Vanessa.

99
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:21,633
-[chickens clucking]
-[Peppa &amp; George giggling]

100
00:04:23,366 --> 00:04:25,300
Boiled eggs for everyone.

101
00:04:25,366 --> 00:04:26,633
[Peppa &amp; George] Hooray!

102
00:04:27,800 --> 00:04:30,766
-Mm. Delicious.
-[snorts]

103
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:35,433
Granny, your chickens make yummy eggs.

104
00:04:35,500 --> 00:04:39,200
Yes. It's all that lovely corn they eat.

105
00:04:39,266 --> 00:04:41,466
And my lettuces.

106
00:04:41,533 --> 00:04:43,533
[all laughing]

107
00:04:47,666 --> 00:04:49,300
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

108
00:04:50,066 --> 00:04:53,000
[narrator] It's the end of another day
at Peppa's playgroup.

109
00:04:53,066 --> 00:04:56,566
Children, tomorrow is Talent Day.

110
00:04:56,633 --> 00:04:58,566
[snorts] What is a talent?

111
00:04:58,633 --> 00:05:02,433
A talent is something you like doing
and you're good at.

112
00:05:02,500 --> 00:05:07,166
[bleats] I like to watch television
and I'm good at it.

113
00:05:07,233 --> 00:05:10,766
Think of something
we might like to see you do.

114
00:05:11,400 --> 00:05:14,300
My talent is playing the guitar.

115
00:05:14,366 --> 00:05:16,366
[playing rock riff]

116
00:05:18,366 --> 00:05:19,700
[all] Ooh.

117
00:05:19,766 --> 00:05:21,033
[parents chatter]

118
00:05:21,099 --> 00:05:23,733
[narrator] The parents have arrived
to pick up the children.

119
00:05:23,800 --> 00:05:27,533
Don't forget to think of something to do
for Talent Day tomorrow.

120
00:05:27,599 --> 00:05:29,533
[plays rock riff]

121
00:05:29,599 --> 00:05:32,333
[narrator] It is bedtime for Peppa
and George.

122
00:05:32,400 --> 00:05:34,466
I can't go to bed yet.

123
00:05:34,533 --> 00:05:37,566
[snorts] I haven't got a talent
to show tomorrow.

124
00:05:37,633 --> 00:05:40,200
But you have lots of talents, Peppa.

125
00:05:40,266 --> 00:05:42,400
Yes. I can skip.

126
00:05:44,166 --> 00:05:45,533
I can sing.

127
00:05:45,599 --> 00:05:48,700
♪ Twinkle, twinkle, little star ♪

128
00:05:48,766 --> 00:05:50,733
I can dance.

129
00:05:50,800 --> 00:05:54,333
[upbeat rock music playing on stereo]

130
00:05:54,800 --> 00:05:57,099
It's hard to choose one talent.

131
00:05:57,166 --> 00:05:59,400
I am good at lots of things.

132
00:05:59,466 --> 00:06:01,166
Don't worry.

133
00:06:01,233 --> 00:06:03,500
-You can decide tomorrow.
-Okay.

134
00:06:04,566 --> 00:06:05,766
[bell rings]

135
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:07,466
[narrator] It is Talent Day.

136
00:06:07,533 --> 00:06:11,666
My talents are skipping,
singing and dancing.

137
00:06:11,733 --> 00:06:14,566
I practiced them all last night.

138
00:06:14,633 --> 00:06:18,566
I was practicing watching television
last night.

139
00:06:18,633 --> 00:06:20,799
[snorts] That's not a talent.

140
00:06:21,033 --> 00:06:23,133
Madame Gazelle said so.

141
00:06:23,200 --> 00:06:25,099
What can I do, then?

142
00:06:25,166 --> 00:06:28,333
Who would like to show us
their talent first?

143
00:06:28,400 --> 00:06:29,266
[Danny woofs]

144
00:06:29,333 --> 00:06:30,233
Danny Dog?

145
00:06:30,299 --> 00:06:32,066
I can bang a drum.

146
00:06:34,666 --> 00:06:36,433
I can bang it louder.

147
00:06:36,500 --> 00:06:38,766
No. That was lovely, Danny.

148
00:06:40,200 --> 00:06:44,266
-[Pedro neighs]
-Pedro Pony, what is your talent?

149
00:06:44,333 --> 00:06:46,799
Magic tricks. [clears throat]

150
00:06:47,033 --> 00:06:49,666
Here is a glass of water.

151
00:06:50,533 --> 00:06:52,733
It is wet and see-through.

152
00:06:52,799 --> 00:06:54,166
[students] Ahh.

153
00:06:54,233 --> 00:06:58,400
Now I will make the water disappear.

154
00:06:58,466 --> 00:07:00,066
[students] Ooh.

155
00:07:00,133 --> 00:07:03,033
Please close your eyes.

156
00:07:06,366 --> 00:07:08,133
Open your eyes.

157
00:07:08,566 --> 00:07:09,466
[students gasp]

158
00:07:09,533 --> 00:07:11,033
[narrator] The water has gone.

159
00:07:12,200 --> 00:07:13,166
Thank you.

160
00:07:13,233 --> 00:07:14,333
[Emily trumpets]

161
00:07:14,400 --> 00:07:15,733
Emily Elephant.

162
00:07:15,799 --> 00:07:18,133
I'm going to play the recorder.

163
00:07:18,766 --> 00:07:22,033
[playing "Twinkle, Twinkle, Little Star"]

164
00:07:24,033 --> 00:07:26,666
-[Rebecca squeaks]
-And what is your talent, Rebecca?

165
00:07:26,733 --> 00:07:29,400
I can make a special noise.

166
00:07:29,466 --> 00:07:31,166
[trills]

167
00:07:31,233 --> 00:07:35,099
It only works if I go up on my tiptoes.

168
00:07:35,166 --> 00:07:37,166
[trilling]

169
00:07:38,133 --> 00:07:40,000
That was very good.

170
00:07:40,066 --> 00:07:42,366
Yes, but what can I do?

171
00:07:42,433 --> 00:07:45,099
Candy, what is your talent?

172
00:07:45,166 --> 00:07:46,333
Skipping.

173
00:07:49,633 --> 00:07:52,466
I was going to do skipping.

174
00:07:52,533 --> 00:07:55,633
But I can still do dancing and singing.

175
00:07:56,266 --> 00:07:58,766
My talent is singing.

176
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:03,299
♪ Twinkle, twinkle, little star ♪

177
00:08:04,700 --> 00:08:07,366
I can still do dancing.

178
00:08:07,433 --> 00:08:10,733
[Madame Gazelle] Suzy Sheep,
what is your talent?

179
00:08:10,799 --> 00:08:12,166
Dancing.

180
00:08:12,233 --> 00:08:14,733
No, you can't dance.

181
00:08:14,799 --> 00:08:18,599
[narrator] Oh, dear.
Dancing was Peppa's last talent.

182
00:08:19,166 --> 00:08:21,500
[band playing
"Twinkle, Twinkle, Little Star"]

183
00:08:28,133 --> 00:08:33,666
It is so nice that everyone has chosen
a different talent to perform.

184
00:08:33,733 --> 00:08:36,533
Now, who do we have left? Peppa.

185
00:08:36,600 --> 00:08:42,333
I was going to skip or sing or dance,
but they've all been done.

186
00:08:42,400 --> 00:08:45,033
A talent can be anything, Peppa.

187
00:08:45,100 --> 00:08:48,100
But not watching television.

188
00:08:48,166 --> 00:08:51,233
Think of something you really like to do.

189
00:08:51,300 --> 00:08:53,000
[snorts] I know.

190
00:08:53,066 --> 00:08:56,266
I've got a talent that I'm really good at.

191
00:08:56,333 --> 00:08:59,066
[narrator] I wonder
what Peppa's talent can be.

192
00:08:59,533 --> 00:09:04,433
My special talent that I am the best at
in the whole world

193
00:09:04,500 --> 00:09:09,366
is jumping up and down
in muddy puddles! [giggling]

194
00:09:09,433 --> 00:09:12,500
[narrator] Peppa loves jumping up and down
in muddy puddles.

195
00:09:13,133 --> 00:09:16,266
Everyone loves jumping up and down
in muddy puddles.

196
00:09:19,500 --> 00:09:21,300
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

197
00:09:21,800 --> 00:09:24,033
[narrator] It is a lovely sunny day.

198
00:09:24,533 --> 00:09:27,233
Peppa is playing with her bouncy ball.

199
00:09:27,300 --> 00:09:31,766
George and his friend Edmond Elephant
are playing with their space toys.

200
00:09:32,366 --> 00:09:33,466
[George &amp; Edmond giggle]

201
00:09:33,533 --> 00:09:35,133
Moon! Moon!

202
00:09:35,199 --> 00:09:38,366
[narrator] George is pretending
that the bouncy ball is the moon.

203
00:09:38,433 --> 00:09:40,666
[snorts] I was playing with that ball.

204
00:09:41,433 --> 00:09:42,566
Oh!

205
00:09:42,633 --> 00:09:45,466
[narrator] Edmond's space toy has landed
on Peppa's head.

206
00:09:45,533 --> 00:09:48,000
-[George &amp; Edmond laugh]
-[laughs] This looks fun.

207
00:09:48,066 --> 00:09:49,233
Are you going to the moon?

208
00:09:49,300 --> 00:09:50,166
[George snorts]

209
00:09:50,233 --> 00:09:55,199
It's just boring space stuff for babies,
Daddy. It's not real.

210
00:09:55,666 --> 00:09:57,433
But space is real, Peppa,

211
00:09:57,500 --> 00:10:00,600
and there are real rockets
that go to the moon.

212
00:10:00,666 --> 00:10:03,733
The museum has a show all about the moon.

213
00:10:03,800 --> 00:10:06,166
-Should we go and see it?
-[George &amp; Edmond] Yay!

214
00:10:06,233 --> 00:10:08,566
Will we really have to go to the moon?

215
00:10:08,633 --> 00:10:11,466
No, Peppa. We're not going to the moon.

216
00:10:11,533 --> 00:10:13,233
We're going to the museum.

217
00:10:13,300 --> 00:10:14,366
Okay.

218
00:10:15,600 --> 00:10:17,233
[narrator] Here is the museum.

219
00:10:17,300 --> 00:10:18,333
[all laugh]

220
00:10:18,800 --> 00:10:21,633
Hello, everyone.
Have you come to see the moon show?

221
00:10:21,699 --> 00:10:23,166
[snorts] Yes, Miss Rabbit.

222
00:10:23,233 --> 00:10:24,733
Five tickets, please.

223
00:10:25,633 --> 00:10:26,699
There you are.

224
00:10:27,300 --> 00:10:29,633
Enjoy your trip to the moon.

225
00:10:29,699 --> 00:10:33,000
Oh, we really are going to the moon.

226
00:10:33,066 --> 00:10:35,633
No, Peppa. It's just pretend.

227
00:10:35,699 --> 00:10:39,133
This way for A Trip to the Moon.

228
00:10:39,199 --> 00:10:41,366
[narrator] Mr. Rabbit is the tour guide.

229
00:10:41,433 --> 00:10:43,166
[children] Ooh.

230
00:10:43,233 --> 00:10:45,233
Prepare for takeoff.

231
00:10:45,300 --> 00:10:47,766
[snorts] It's just pretend, isn't it?

232
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:50,433
That's right, Peppa. It's just pretend.

233
00:10:50,500 --> 00:10:55,333
[man on recording]
Five, four, three, two, one.

234
00:10:56,133 --> 00:10:57,166
Blastoff.

235
00:11:00,100 --> 00:11:01,666
We live on a planet.

236
00:11:02,133 --> 00:11:05,199
-Does anyone know what it is called?
-The Earth.

237
00:11:05,266 --> 00:11:06,533
That's right.

238
00:11:06,600 --> 00:11:10,600
Oh-ho. I'm a bit of an expert
at space things.

239
00:11:10,666 --> 00:11:14,266
There are seven other planets
that go around our sun.

240
00:11:14,333 --> 00:11:16,466
Does anyone know what they are called?

241
00:11:16,533 --> 00:11:17,633
Uh...

242
00:11:17,699 --> 00:11:20,766
-Mercury.
-Ooh. Well done, Edmond.

243
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:26,400
Venus, Mars, Jupiter, Saturn,
Neptune, Uranus.

244
00:11:26,466 --> 00:11:29,066
[narrator] Edmond knows all about space.

245
00:11:29,133 --> 00:11:30,766
I'm a clever clogs.

246
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:32,199
[Edmond trumpets]

247
00:11:32,266 --> 00:11:33,233
[all laugh]

248
00:11:33,300 --> 00:11:36,233
Does anyone know what these planets
are made off?

249
00:11:37,066 --> 00:11:38,633
They're made of cardboard.

250
00:11:38,699 --> 00:11:41,066
[Mr. Rabbit] These models are made
of cardboard,

251
00:11:41,133 --> 00:11:45,266
but the real planets are made of rock
and ice and gas.

252
00:11:45,800 --> 00:11:48,533
But of course, the moon is made of cheese.

253
00:11:48,600 --> 00:11:50,066
[all laugh]

254
00:11:50,133 --> 00:11:54,100
No, the moon is made of rock,
and this is a serious tour.

255
00:11:54,166 --> 00:11:56,500
So, no jokes and no giggling.

256
00:11:58,166 --> 00:12:00,500
Here we are, on the moon.

257
00:12:00,566 --> 00:12:03,733
It's a pretend moon really, isn't it?

258
00:12:03,800 --> 00:12:08,600
Yes. If this was the real moon,
you could jump over my head.

259
00:12:08,666 --> 00:12:09,800
Ooh.

260
00:12:10,033 --> 00:12:13,566
Does anyone know
why we can jump so high on the moon?

261
00:12:13,633 --> 00:12:14,733
Gravity.

262
00:12:14,800 --> 00:12:16,766
Oh, that's right, Edmond.

263
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:20,199
Gravity is what keeps us on the ground.

264
00:12:20,266 --> 00:12:23,666
It is weaker on the moon,
so, you can jump higher.

265
00:12:23,733 --> 00:12:25,166
[Edmond &amp; pigs] Ooh.

266
00:12:25,233 --> 00:12:30,166
We can make you feel like you're jumping
on the moon with the help of science.

267
00:12:30,233 --> 00:12:33,633
That sounds impressive.
How do you do that?

268
00:12:33,699 --> 00:12:36,099
With big rubber bands.

269
00:12:37,233 --> 00:12:41,066
[narrator] Everyone's strapped into
Mr. Rabbit's Antigravity Rubber Bands.

270
00:12:41,133 --> 00:12:43,000
[all laughing]

271
00:12:45,400 --> 00:12:48,466
[narrator] Bouncing on the pretend moon
is fun.

272
00:12:49,099 --> 00:12:50,599
Say "Moon cheese."

273
00:12:50,666 --> 00:12:52,633
[all] Moon Cheese.

274
00:12:54,633 --> 00:12:58,400
And that is the end of the tour.
Please walk this way.

275
00:12:58,466 --> 00:13:01,466
-Are there trees on the moon?
-No.

276
00:13:01,533 --> 00:13:03,466
Are there any cars on the moon?

277
00:13:03,533 --> 00:13:04,533
No.

278
00:13:04,599 --> 00:13:06,800
Are there any moon shops?

279
00:13:07,033 --> 00:13:09,066
No, that would be silly.

280
00:13:09,133 --> 00:13:11,099
Welcome to the moon shop.

281
00:13:11,166 --> 00:13:13,533
We've got moon maps, moon books,

282
00:13:13,599 --> 00:13:17,000
even a picture of piggies on the moon
with an elephant.

283
00:13:17,066 --> 00:13:20,533
[snorts] Look, there we are
jumping on the moon.

284
00:13:20,599 --> 00:13:22,533
We've got moon rock, too.

285
00:13:22,599 --> 00:13:25,500
It's got a picture of the moon
through the middle.

286
00:13:25,566 --> 00:13:27,033
[Peppa] Ooh.

287
00:13:27,099 --> 00:13:29,300
How about some real moon cheese?

288
00:13:29,366 --> 00:13:31,266
How much is it, Miss Rabbit?

289
00:13:31,333 --> 00:13:33,033
Five pounds, please.

290
00:13:33,500 --> 00:13:35,099
Five pounds?

291
00:13:35,166 --> 00:13:37,433
It's all for a good cause.

292
00:13:37,500 --> 00:13:41,366
I like the moon now
because it's very interesting.

293
00:13:41,433 --> 00:13:42,699
Mm.

294
00:13:42,766 --> 00:13:44,433
And very tasty.

295
00:13:45,066 --> 00:13:47,066
[all laughing]

296
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:51,000
[children giggling]

297
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:54,099
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

298
00:13:55,233 --> 00:13:58,166
[narrator] Grandpa Pig
is looking after Peppa and George.

299
00:13:58,233 --> 00:14:03,233
Now, Grandpa,
I will tell you how everything works.

300
00:14:03,300 --> 00:14:05,500
-[snorts] This is the slide.
-Whee!

301
00:14:05,566 --> 00:14:09,233
You climb up here
and you slide down there.

302
00:14:09,300 --> 00:14:10,466
Whee!

303
00:14:10,533 --> 00:14:13,466
[Peppa] And everyone takes it in turns.

304
00:14:13,533 --> 00:14:15,199
-[Grandpa Pig snorts] Ho-ho!
-Whee!

305
00:14:15,266 --> 00:14:18,199
I know what a slide is, Peppa.

306
00:14:18,266 --> 00:14:22,533
I used to play on one myself
when I was a little piggy.

307
00:14:22,599 --> 00:14:26,466
Did you have swings, too,
in the olden days?

308
00:14:26,533 --> 00:14:32,800
Ho-ho! We had swings and climbing frames
and roundabouts.

309
00:14:33,033 --> 00:14:37,166
-Oh!
-But my favorite was the slide.

310
00:14:37,233 --> 00:14:39,166
It is my favorite, too.

311
00:14:39,233 --> 00:14:41,699
[Peppa giggles, then snorts] Whee!

312
00:14:41,766 --> 00:14:45,033
[narrator] Everyone takes it in turns
to have a go on the slide.

313
00:14:45,099 --> 00:14:48,666
Whee! [giggles]

314
00:14:48,733 --> 00:14:52,633
Naughty Richard.
You know you have to wait your turn.

315
00:14:52,699 --> 00:14:55,599
[narrator] Richard Rabbit finds it hard
to wait his turn.

316
00:14:55,666 --> 00:14:58,133
[Richard crying]

317
00:14:58,199 --> 00:14:59,533
Oh, dear.

318
00:14:59,599 --> 00:15:03,166
It's not easy being small, is it, Richard?

319
00:15:03,233 --> 00:15:04,099
[Richard sobs]

320
00:15:04,166 --> 00:15:08,800
[snorts] Because Richard is little,
I don't think he should have to wait.

321
00:15:09,033 --> 00:15:12,300
I wouldn't change the rules if I were you,
Grandpa Pig.

322
00:15:12,366 --> 00:15:13,433
Nonsense.

323
00:15:13,500 --> 00:15:16,366
The children understand, don't you?

324
00:15:16,433 --> 00:15:17,633
[Richard giggling]

325
00:15:18,733 --> 00:15:19,733
Whee!

326
00:15:19,800 --> 00:15:24,500
But, Grandpa, George is little
and he has to wait his turn.

327
00:15:24,566 --> 00:15:26,400
[George crying]

328
00:15:26,466 --> 00:15:29,533
Yes, George is little.

329
00:15:29,599 --> 00:15:31,800
So, he shouldn't have to wait either.

330
00:15:32,033 --> 00:15:34,400
[George giggles] Whee!

331
00:15:35,033 --> 00:15:35,733
[Richard giggles]

332
00:15:35,800 --> 00:15:40,000
[narrator] Oh, dear. Richard and George
are taking all the turns on the slide.

333
00:15:40,066 --> 00:15:43,533
Grandpa,
when do we get to go on the slide?

334
00:15:43,599 --> 00:15:45,400
Don't worry, Peppa.

335
00:15:45,466 --> 00:15:48,233
They won't be on it for long.

336
00:15:48,300 --> 00:15:51,500
[sighs] I'm bored of waiting.

337
00:15:51,566 --> 00:15:54,366
Me, too. Let's play on the swing.

338
00:15:54,433 --> 00:15:56,500
[children giggling]

339
00:15:56,566 --> 00:15:59,000
[narrator] Here is Pedro Pony
on the swing.

340
00:15:59,066 --> 00:15:59,766
[Pedro neighs]

341
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:02,633
[snorts] Pedro, can I have a go now?

342
00:16:02,699 --> 00:16:05,800
I just want to swing a bit more.

343
00:16:06,033 --> 00:16:09,133
But you've been on the swing for ages.

344
00:16:09,199 --> 00:16:13,433
Grandpa Pig, can you push me a little bit,
please?

345
00:16:13,500 --> 00:16:17,333
I think it is someone else's turn now,
Pedro.

346
00:16:17,400 --> 00:16:20,066
But I have to go home soon.

347
00:16:20,133 --> 00:16:22,766
Oh, I see. That's different.

348
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:24,433
Let me push you, then.

349
00:16:24,500 --> 00:16:26,199
But, Grandpa.

350
00:16:26,266 --> 00:16:28,533
[Pedro giggling]

351
00:16:28,599 --> 00:16:31,133
I'm bored of waiting.

352
00:16:31,199 --> 00:16:33,099
-Me, too.
-And me.

353
00:16:33,166 --> 00:16:35,800
[woofs] Let's play on the roundabout.

354
00:16:36,400 --> 00:16:38,766
[narrator] Everyone wants to get
on the roundabout.

355
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:42,033
Too many children on the roundabout.

356
00:16:42,099 --> 00:16:43,466
Everybody off.

357
00:16:43,533 --> 00:16:44,633
[children sigh]

358
00:16:44,699 --> 00:16:48,133
But, Grandpa Pig,
I was actually here first.

359
00:16:48,199 --> 00:16:52,066
Ah. Then you can get back
on the roundabout.

360
00:16:52,133 --> 00:16:53,800
I need to get on, too.

361
00:16:54,033 --> 00:16:56,033
Oh, why's that, Rebecca?

362
00:16:56,099 --> 00:17:00,000
Um... because it's my birthday soon.

363
00:17:00,066 --> 00:17:02,466
-Oh. Oh, okay.
-[Rebecca giggles]

364
00:17:02,533 --> 00:17:04,566
-[girls] And me.
-All right.

365
00:17:04,633 --> 00:17:05,500
[girls giggle]

366
00:17:05,566 --> 00:17:07,433
Is everybody ready?

367
00:17:07,500 --> 00:17:08,366
[girls] Yes.

368
00:17:08,433 --> 00:17:12,200
[woofs] Stop.
There are no boys on the roundabout.

369
00:17:12,266 --> 00:17:14,500
-Um...
-[Danny giggles]

370
00:17:14,566 --> 00:17:17,533
Now is everybody ready?

371
00:17:17,599 --> 00:17:19,633
I'm wearing glasses.

372
00:17:19,700 --> 00:17:21,666
Can I go on, please?

373
00:17:21,733 --> 00:17:24,366
[narrator] The children are making up
their own rules.

374
00:17:24,433 --> 00:17:28,133
I need to get on
because I like carrots. [giggles]

375
00:17:28,200 --> 00:17:31,399
Now are you all ready to go?

376
00:17:31,466 --> 00:17:35,333
No. I have to get on
because I can do this:

377
00:17:35,399 --> 00:17:36,266
[blows raspberry]

378
00:17:36,333 --> 00:17:38,333
[children giggling]

379
00:17:38,733 --> 00:17:40,333
[narrator] Here is Mommy Pig.

380
00:17:40,399 --> 00:17:42,600
[snorts] How are you getting on,
Grandpa Pig?

381
00:17:42,666 --> 00:17:45,000
I'm confused.

382
00:17:45,066 --> 00:17:48,800
These playground rules
are too complicated.

383
00:17:49,033 --> 00:17:51,600
There is only one rule, Grandpa Pig,

384
00:17:51,666 --> 00:17:55,533
and that is everyone waits their turn.

385
00:17:55,600 --> 00:17:57,600
Whee! [giggles]

386
00:17:57,666 --> 00:18:00,433
What? Even the little ones?

387
00:18:00,500 --> 00:18:02,333
[Mommy Pig] Even the little ones.

388
00:18:02,399 --> 00:18:06,800
What about the very old ones like Grandpa?

389
00:18:07,033 --> 00:18:09,500
Even the very old ones like Grandpa.

390
00:18:09,566 --> 00:18:13,033
[narrator] At the playground,
everyone has their turn.

391
00:18:13,100 --> 00:18:15,033
Whee!

392
00:18:15,100 --> 00:18:17,100
[all laughing]

393
00:18:20,100 --> 00:18:21,466
-[child giggles]
-[Peppa snorts]

394
00:18:21,533 --> 00:18:22,800
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

395
00:18:23,033 --> 00:18:25,100
-[Peppa snorts]
-[child giggles]

396
00:18:25,166 --> 00:18:26,033
[Peppa snorts]

397
00:18:26,100 --> 00:18:27,600
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

398
00:18:27,666 --> 00:18:30,166
-[Peppa snorts]
-[children giggle]

399
00:18:30,233 --> 00:18:31,666
♪ Peppa Pig ♪

400
00:18:31,733 --> 00:18:33,366
-[Peppa snorts]
-[children giggle]

